    ],
    "why": {
      "FLAT.2": "The champion's label, mucinous cystadenocarcinoma of the liver, matches the preoperative diagnosis made based on imaging findings, including abdominal CT, MRI, abdominal ultrasound, and PET–CT, which showed a well-defined, low-density, heterogeneous, multilocular cystic tumor with septa, an enhancing solid compartment, and a nonenhancing cystic compartment, consistent with the champion's label."
    }
  },
